{
  "slug": "vibe-thesis",
  "name": "Vibe Thesis",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "Academic thesis authoring in Claude Code. vibe-thesis scaffolds and co-authors thesis-shaped artifacts — dissertations, master's theses, long-form research articles, position essays — with a rendered PDF skeleton in about 30 minutes. Its voice pipeline captures whose prose anchors your writing and applies it to drafts without changing your claims, while a tone lint catches the inflationary, self-praising patterns LLM-assisted academic writing tends to accumulate. Six commands: render, status, voice, guard, smooth, audit.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **6 skills** and **5 commands**.\n\n- **Skills** (6): `synthesis-guard` (Lint pass over the project's body content for self-review tone), `synthesis-smooth` (Apply the project's voice profile to a draft markdown file), `vibe-render` (Render the current Vibe Thesis project (PDF, HTML, markdown, or all)), `vibe-status` (Compose a one-screen summary of the current Vibe Thesis project: title and mode, planning docs presence, body content…), `vibe-thesis` (Use when the user wants to scaffold a thesis-shaped project (academic dissertation, master's thesis, long-form research article, position…), `voice-synthesis` (Interview the user for author voice synthesis)\n- **Commands** (5): `guard` (Self-review-tone lint over body content), `smooth` (Apply the project's voice profile to a draft markdown file), `vibe-render` (Render the project to PDF, HTML, markdown, or all formats), `vibe-status` (Report the state of the current Vibe Thesis project: planning docs, body content, claim coverage, citations, last render), `voice` (Author voice synthesis)\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install vibe-thesis@claude-community` from `estevanhernandez-stack-ed/Vibe-Thesis` (`plugins/vibe-thesis`).",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude"
  ],
  "pluginType": "package",
  "package": {
    "skill": 6,
    "command": 5
  },
  "sourceType": "community",
  "author": {
    "name": "626Labs LLC"
  },
